  "term": "animal dominance",
  "definition": "Animal dominance refers to the patterned ranking relationships, or pecking orders, that form within groups of animals. In this source, these hierarchies are described not as fixed standings but as dynamic social networks shaped by ongoing sequences of interaction among group members.",
